 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "I thought I had seen the darkness\nThrough some small window of celebration,\nWhen once it fell upon me\nTo see that great calmness begun.\nAnd to think, as my vision\nShook from its splendor away,\nThat my soul now seemed alone,\nIn this lonely night.  Today\nThere were no lights somewhere,\nBut only these shadows, too,\nLike something old and fallen, too,\nWhere in the summer dew",
